# Records of phases 1 and 2 brought up to date after phase 3 — part 3. Assessed against the code on 2026-09-27.
#
# Each record replaces the record of the same number in docs/requirement-status.json (or, for a requirement that
# was PLANNED, its reason in docs/requirement-planned-notes.json). What the earlier record said and is still true
# is carried over; what Phase 3 added is named as such. No status was lowered.
# "Phase 1" and "Phase 2" inside a note mean: built in that phase, and read again in the code for this record.
#
# Facts that apply to many records below (verified in the code):
#   * NUMI answers questions; it never acts. It reads through the data layer of the person who asks and checks the
#     permission before it reads. Which sentence reaches which answer is decided by the patterns in
#     src/numi/engine.ts, src/numi/ops.ts and src/numi/p3.ts; a sentence that matches none gets the list of what
#     NUMI can answer. The sentences quoted in the notes were read against those patterns one by one.
#   * A spoken or typed command is read by src/voice/commands.ts. A verb that changes the books, moves money or
#     sends a message is never carried out: the screen is opened for the person.
#   * Nothing runs on a schedule and nothing leaves the application. A rule of Sentinel runs when a person presses
#     'Run Sentinel now' or saves a record; a notice is looked for when a person opens the application.
#   * An alert is what Sentinel shows. NUMERO Reality compares records and lists differences; a difference raises
#     no alert. A physical verification and a confirmation raise an alert for what they find.
#   * The screens were read in the code. None was driven against the live database.
